# A permutation model of the Fischer group `Fi₂₂`

This file defines a permutation model `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22` of the Fischer group `Fi₂₂`: the
subgroup of `Equiv.Perm (Fin 3510)` generated by two explicit permutations `Fi22.a` and `Fi22.b`,
each of order `13`. In the Fischer group `Fi₂₂` the `3`-transpositions form a conjugacy class of
`3510` involutions, the centralizer of one of them being a maximal subgroup of shape `2·U₆(2)`,
and `3510` is the least degree in which that group acts faithfully; the model is meant as its
action by conjugation on that class.

The two permutations are given by their tables of images, and the point `i` of `Fin 3510` is the
point `i` of the source of the tables (see *Provenance*). Products follow Mathlib's convention
`(σ * τ) x = σ (τ x)`.

Neither the order of the model nor its transitivity or simplicity is asserted here. The generators
are not the standard generators of `Fi₂₂`, which have orders `2` and `13`: the module
`TauCeti.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.Sporadic.Fischer.TwentyTwo.Presentation` gives two
permutations of those orders that generate the model and satisfy the relators of the presentation
of `Fi₂₂` on its standard generators, and so maps the presented group onto the model.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22`: the permutation model of the Fischer group `Fi₂₂` on `3510` points.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.orderOf_a`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Fi22.orderOf_b`: both generators have
  order `13`.

## Provenance

The tables of `Fi22.a` and `Fi22.b` are those of the permutations `fi22a` and `fi22b` of the
`FiniteSimpleGroups` project (Apache-2.0), file `FiniteSimpleGroups/Sporadic/Fi22/Basic.lean` at
commit `7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`. That file stores the two permutations and their
inverses as the natural numbers `fi22aFlat`, `fi22aInvFlat`, `fi22bFlat` and `fi22bInvFlat`, the
image of the point `i` being the field `i` of width `12`. The four tables below are these four
natural numbers, written in base `2 ^ 360`, so the numbering of the points is unchanged. The
source describes the points as the `3`-transpositions of `Fi₂₂`, obtained there as the vertices of
a strongly regular graph with parameters `(3510, 693, 180, 126)` built from the `693` isotropic
points of the hermitian space of dimension `6` over the field with four elements. The definitions
of the two permutations are taken from the source; its proofs of the order and the simplicity of
the generated group are not reproduced here.

## References

* KitaKen1 (Kenta), *FiniteSimpleGroups*, `Fi22` construction at commit
  `7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`,
  <https://github.com/KitaKen1/finite-simple-groups-lean>.
* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, the page of `Fi₂₂`, for the maximal subgroup `2·U₆(2)` of index `3510`,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/spor/F22/>.
-/

