/- Each generator is given by the table of its images and the table of its preimages. A table has
117 rows, each a hexadecimal numeral of 90 digits holding 30 entries of three digits: the entry of
the point `30 * r + j` is the group of three digits of row `r` in position `j` counted from the
right, starting at zero. The table is the natural number having the rows as its digits in base
`2 ^ 360`, so that the entry of the point `i` is field `i` of width `12` of that number. The
kernel reads such a field by binary arithmetic in one step, whereas a lookup in a list or an
array costs one reduction for every position passed.

The bodies are exposed so that importing modules can compute with the two permutations. -/

/-- The first generator of the permutation model of the Fischer group `Fi₂₂`, a permutation of
order `13` of the `3510` points. Entry `i` of the first table is the image of the point `i`, and
entry `i` of the second table is its preimage. -/
